    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10139": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - School of Chemistry - 108046 - Grade 7",
      "description": "Based in the School of Chemistry, you will work with Dr Dominik Kubicki and Birmingham's Facility for Electron Microscopy, alongside protein scientists, materials chemists and engineers. You will develop the microscopy and image-analysis workflows that reveal how protein assembly and the microstructure of the materials that they fabricate. Your evidence will guide which materials the team redesigns, advances and scales up.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-03",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10140": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Department of Metabolism and Systems Science - 107881 - Grade 7",
      "description": "The postholder will work within a recently awarded grant from the Paradifference Foundation, a charity set up with the purpose of finding new treatments for SDHB-deficient cancers. The postholder will work alongside others in a dynamic and ambitious research group led by Professor Tennant, and in addition to their own project will have the opportunity to contribute to other research projects within the group. \n\nPosting closes: 2026-10-27",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10143": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - NMR - School of Chemistry - 108102 - Grade 7",
      "description": "As Research Fellow, you will apply nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectroscopy and imaging to generate new knowledge and understanding of how ions are stored electrochemically in carbonaceous materials. As part of an interdisciplinary team within the group of Professor Melanie Britton at the University of Birmingham, and in collaboration with scientists from the Schools of Chemistry and Metallurgy and Materials, you will work to deliver the objectives of an Leverhulme Trust Research Grant “A unified model of electrochemical ion-storage in carbon”.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-10-20",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10145": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Synthetic Supramolecular Chemistry - School of Chemistry - 107945 - Grade 7",
      "description": "The School of Chemistry seeks to attract outstanding, inspirational and talented people, supporting them to succeed and celebrating their success. We value diversity and inclusion and welcome applications from all sections of the community. The School of Chemistry holds an Athena SWAN Silver Award, in recognition of its work in promoting women’s careers in higher education. The University of Birmingham is a member institution of the Race Equality Charter, a Disability Confident Employer and contributes to the Stonewall Workplace Equality Index. We support flexible working and studying.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-03",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10162": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - School of Engineering - 55027 - Grade 7",
      "description": "To support a range of ionospheric projects, SERENE is looking to welcome an outstanding candidate to work in the field of ionospheric data assimilation modelling.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-03",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10175": {
      "title": "Marie Sklodowska-Curie Doctoral Researcher - Mechanical Engineering - 108121 - Grade 8",
      "description": "To create and disseminate knowledge through initiating and conducting original research and through publication, as appropriate to the disciplinary area. The posts are part of SurPhase, a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Network funded under Horizon Europe (Grant Agreement No. 101311533) and coordinated by the University of Birmingham.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-15",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10202": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Sustainable Manufacturing of Functional Ceramics) - School of Metallurgy and Materials - 108128 - Grade 7",
      "description": "The postholder will play a leading role in these recycling activities and be responsible for assessing the elemental quantities of the materials as part of initial characterisation studies, to the safe disassembly and recovery of materials. The successful candidate will apply a range of recycling tools to separate the feedstocks and to restore functionality of the materials. The candidate will play an active role in data collection inputs/outputs to support the life cycle assessments to evaluate the recycling pathway of these functional materials.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-17",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10222": {
      "title": "Research Associate - School of Psychology - 108209 - Grade 6",
      "description": "The postholder will work as part of a multidisciplinary research team delivering a randomised controlled trial (RCT) investigating arts and culture for mental health in young people in collaboration with a Clinical Trials Unit (CTU). The study involves community based recruitment, meaningful youth involvement, and a qualitative process evaluation within the trial. The post will provide research and administrative support to ensure successful delivery of the project.\n\n\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-03",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10242": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Department of Cardiovascular Sciences - 108207 - Grade 7",
      "description": "This position is based within the research group of Professor Melanie Madhani in the Department of Cardiovascular Sciences at the University of Birmingham. The post will focus on identifying and developing novel therapeutic approaches for the treatment of hypertension. \n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-09",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10228": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow - Department of Applied Health Sciences - 108206 - Grade 7",
      "description": "The post holder will join Bright at an exciting time following the completion of the first year of the MSc and external funding secured to grow our postgraduate education portfolio with three new modules regarding AI in cancer diagnostics and global software medical device regulation. The team is also highly active in research and policy, with an established track record for high impact research outputs. This post will present opportunities to engage with some of these research projects where they align with the post holder’s interests and goals for professional development.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-10-28",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10251": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Department of Pharmacy - 107639 - Grade 7",
      "description": "To create and contribute to the creation of knowledge by undertaking a specified range of  activities within a funded MRC New Investigator Research Grant on ‘Targeting lysine metabolism for treatment of epilepsy in tuberous sclerosis complex’.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-09",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10260": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Electronic, Electrical, and Systems Engineering",
      "description": "We are seeking an ambitious researcher ready to transition into the next step of their career. Your interest will lie in frontier technologies of electrical, electronic and computer engineering; applications are welcomed from candidates with expertise in one or more of the following or closely related technologies: computing, data, and intelligence; electromagnetic, aerospace, and defence; robotics and autonomy; applied physics; advanced materials, devices, and components; sustainable energy technologies; human experience and augmentation; smart connected and integrated systems; electrical engineering education advancement.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-30",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/9345": {
      "title": "Research fellow (EPSRC Funded CLEETS Project) - School of Geography, Earth and Environmental Sciences - 107469 - Grade 7",
      "description": "The successful candidate will join a multidisciplinary research team based at the University of Birmingham and will work closely with collaborators at Cardiff University and partner institutions in the USA. The primary aim of this role is to advance understanding of the societal impacts of transport decarbonisation strategies and energy system transitions in urban regions in both the United States (Great Lakes) and the United Kingdom (South Wales and the West Midlands). \nThe postholder will undertake travel demand analysis using attitudinal and stated preference data collected by the CLEETS team, with a focus on examining transport users’ awareness of environmental impacts and how this influences their adoption of sustainable travel choices. The role will also involve close engagement with a wide range of stakeholders to understand policy priorities at both regional and national levels.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-02",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10206": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - School of Engineering - 106915 - Grade 7",
      "description": "FractureFix is a UKRI EPSRC funded International Centre to Centre Award concerned with research investigating secondary osteoporosis and bone fracture. \nIt comprises a collaboration between the University of Birmingham (Lead organisation), ETH Zurich, Switzerland and Uppsala University, Sweden. Within this consortium, the role is to investigate novel interventions to either prevent or reduce the effects of fracture.\n\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-10",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10210": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - School of Engineering - 108142 - Grade 7",
      "description": "OncoEng is a UKRI EPSRC funded flagship programme grant concerned with research into interventions for metastatic bone disease in the spine.  It comprises a collaboration between the University of Birmingham (Lead organisation), Imperial College London, University of Leeds University College London. With this consortium the role aims to develop and implement new techniques to assess long term fatigue and fracture mechanisms within metastatic infiltrated spinal vertebrae and how these fractures may be prevented using novel minimally invasive implants.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-01",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10209": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Department of Cancer and Genomic Sciences, - 107560 - Grade 7",
      "description": "The Department of Cancer and Genomic Sciences at the University of Birmingham is seeking an exceptional candidate for a research position in the Morris lab to undertake fundamental research in DNA replication and DNA damage and repair. The post holder will investigate how replication fork transitions are regulated and balanced. They will create and contribute to knowledge by addressing how critical transition points in DNA replication stalling are controlled and relate to topological differences in DNA using cell biological approaches, and advanced microscopy and/ or biophysical approaches.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-09",
      "department": null
    }
  },
